<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koźle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cosel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Koźle is a historic town on the Oder in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, now part of the city of Kędzierzyn-Koźle. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the seat of a small Silesian Piast duchy, and under Prussian rule it became a fortress, besieged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s allies in 1807. Its river port on the Oder later grew into one of the largest inland harbours in the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kozle.jpg" alt="Koźle" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LuzynaS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ko%C5%BAle,_Rynek_z_fontann%C4%85.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
